extraction_notes: "WB19 Australia printed 107-110 (cache p108-p111, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer in column order. The entry heading Cyber-Specter O.C.C. and its lore start in the second column of printed 107; the Special Cyber-Specter O.C.C. Bonuses & Abilities start on printed 108 and run onto 109; the stat block is on printed 109 and ends with Standard Equipment, Money and Cybernetics on printed 110. The City O.C.C. list on printed 105 spells it Cyber-Spectre. || HEADING: no NPC or villain heading, so no evil tag. Listed under Optional City O.C.C.s on printed 105, so occ_group is optional. The class prints its own Base S.D.C. (4D6), so no men_of_arms line is needed. || XP: the City Administrator, Cyber-Specter, Police TRG ladder on the Experience Tables, printed 224, read off a render. || BONUSES (ability 1): +2 I.Q., +1 M.E. and +1 on initiative stored. || COMPUTER HACKING: the page disagrees with itself. Ability 2 (printed 108) prints Base Skill 15% +5% per level plus a +25% bonus, so he really starts at 40%; the O.C.C. skill list (printed 109) prints Computer Hacking (+30%), which would be 45%. Stored at 40, the figure the ability spells out. The modifier table and the trace rules are special_abilities prose; nothing in them is applied by the sheet. The text layer prints several times as !D6xlO, 2D4xlO, 2D4xlOO and 3D6xlOO; they are 1D6x10, 2D4x10, 2D4x100 and 3D6x100. The page prints TGR once for TRG. || SKILLS: Speaks English at 96% is Language: Australian English at 96 with no per-level gain. Literacy (+30%) is Literacy: Native Language at 70. Writing (+8%) is the catalog row Creative Writing at 33. Radio: Scrambler is Radio: Scramblers; Radio: Cryptography is the row Cryptography. Hand to Hand: none to start; Basic costs one related skill, Expert two, Martial Arts or Assassin four. || RELATED: ten at level one and two more at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Military, Rogue and Wilderness are printed None and left out; the list has no Cowboy line. || MONEY: personal savings of 2D4x100 dollars stored (Australian dollars equal credits). The monthly salary of about 1D4x1,000 from a mundane day job (printed lD4x$ 1,000), or 2-5 times that from a computer job, is in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: wristwatch, the packet of Everwake stimulants, painkillers and the illegal books on computer code have no row. The 1D4+1 electronic gadgets rolled or chosen from a list of ten are in GM Notes, because a choice with a rolled quantity cannot be stored. The light anti-assassin vest (at the G.M.''s option), the simple ground vehicle and the two room apartment are in GM Notes. The desktop computer is stored as the nearest row, Computer, Portable. || NOT STORED: the note that a Psi-Ghost or Psi-Tech (World Book 12: Psyscape) may take this class''s skills and background with O.C.C. Related and Secondary skills halved is in GM Notes."
